DTSTAMP:20260630T005220Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260702
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260708
SUMMARY:Jason: Philadelphia\, PA
DESCRIPTION:NEP Bishops & Media - Philadelphia\n\nStatus: Booked\nHotel: So
 nesta Philadelphia Rittenhouse Square\, event/block NEP Bishops & Media - P
 hiladelphia. Confirmation QQAX2KIP for Jason Shanks.\nStay: arrive Thu Jul
  2\, depart Mon Jul 6. Room type: Deluxe - Two Queens\; 1 room\, 2 guests.
  Rate shown in confirmation: $229/night\; grand total $1\,065.86.\nAmerican
  Airlines reservation GGJXVR: outbound Sat Jul 4 AA 6208 FWA-ORD 5:23-6:35
  AM\, then AA 2115 ORD-PHL 7:37-9:48 AM.\nAmerican Airlines reservation GGJ
 XVR: return Tue Jul 7 AA 3030 PHL-CLT 4:55-6:58 PM\, then AA 5961 CLT-FWA 8
 :33-10:34 PM.\nCancellation: cancel by 4:00 PM local hotel time the day bef
 ore arrival to avoid one night room/tax penalty.\nNEC staff lodging listed
  for Jason Shanks\, Ephrem Shanks\, Sarah Houde\, Maria Benes\, and Haley R
 ossi at Sonesta Rittenhouse Square\, 1800 Market Street\, less than a mile
  from the Cathedral Basilica.\nThu Jul 2: Pilgrim team expected to arrive 3
 :00-4:00 PM\; Father Gill should receive ETA once team is on the road. Jaso
 n and Ephrem's PHL arrival time / AA flight number still TBD.\nThu Jul 2: S
 arah arrives PHL 4:14 PM on DL 5706\; Maria arrives PHL 6:00 PM\, Southwest
  flight number TBD. Sarah will Uber to hotel and meet team at Cathedral Bas
 ilica for dinner.\nThu Jul 2: 5:30 PM dinner at Cathedral Basilica\, then 7
 :00 PM Young Adult Holy Hour. Overnight adoration follows with local adorer
 s filling spots.\nFri Jul 3: Christ in the City service day. 8:30 AM traini
 ng at Cathedral Basilica Neumann Room\; 9:15 AM-noon walk through city cent
 er to visit with homeless\; concludes with 12:05 PM Sung Mass and boxed lun
 ches.\nFri Jul 3 civic options: 11:00 AM Pope Leo Liberty Medal video addre
 ss at Independence Mall\; noon-4:00 PM Salute to Independence parade\; 5:00
  PM food trucks/block party and 7:00-9:00 PM Philly Pops Concert at Indepen
 dence National Historical Park.\nSat Jul 4: Mary Carmen's birthday. Cabrini
  film showings at Cathedral Basilica at 10:00 AM\, 1:00 PM\, and 3:30 PM\,
  though pilgrims already saw the film in Charlotte.\nSat Jul 4: Cathedral d
 ay includes 12:05 PM Sung Mass\, street-fair lunch\, 4:30 PM Family Rosary
  Across America\, 5:15 PM Vigil Mass\, dinner after Mass\, and 7:00 PM NEC
  Staff & Pilgrim Dinner with Relevant Radio. Location still TBD.\nSat Jul 4
  follow-up: confirm when RR is arriving / setting up equipment\; Jason aske
 d if Father Rocky can attend dinner\; invite Archbishop Perez and Bishop Po
 hlmeier once time/location are known.\nSat Jul 4 civic options: Historic Ge
 rmantown all day\; FIFA Fan Festival noon-4:00 PM at Lemon Hill\; World Cup
  game 5:00 PM at Lincoln Financial Field\; Benjamin Franklin Parkway concer
 t/fireworks 5:00 PM-midnight\, fireworks at 11:45 PM.\nSun Jul 5: Cathedral
  revised Mass schedule is 7:30 AM\, 9:00 AM\, 11:00 AM\, 1:00 PM Spanish/Ch
 apel. Confessions at 8:30 AM and 12:30 PM Spanish/Chapel.\nSun Jul 5: team
  arrival time and reserved parking locations still TBD for NEP van\, Rachel
 's car\, and Sarah's parents' car.\nSun Jul 5: 10:50 AM? Pope Leo video add
 ress before 11:00 AM Solemn Mass\; exact time awaiting EWTN confirmation. P
 erpetual Pilgrims bring prayer intentions to altar during offertory.\nSun J
 ul 5: Heavy snacks in Drexel Hall after Mass for pilgrims/staff to pack bef
 ore procession\; no time for lunch before procession.\nSun Jul 5: 12:30 PM
  Eucharistic Procession from Cathedral Basilica to National Shrine of St. J
 ohn Neumann at St. Peter the Apostle Church\; route approx. 2 miles\, concl
 uding with Benediction. NEC banner carried by archdiocesan seminarians Josh
 ua Brooks and Ryan Scavnicky.\nSun Jul 5: 1:30-4:30 PM concluding fellowshi
 p reception at St. Peter the Apostle / Shrine of St. John Neumann\, with 2:
 00 PM press conference during reception. Reception has light appetizers onl
 y\, likely not enough for dinner.\nSun Jul 5 follow-up: decide whether NEC
  should arrange team dinner\; Maria Benes offered to look into a reservatio
 n.\nMon Jul 6: Perpetual Pilgrim team departs for post-NEP retreat at IHM S
 pirituality Center\, 210 IHM Drive\, Malvern\, PA 19355\; departure time TB
 D.\nMon Jul 6: 6:45 PM meet Tim Flanagan in the lobby at Four Seasons Hotel
  Philadelphia\, One N 19th Street. Tim is flying up from Orlando with ETA 5
 :15 PM and will advise if delayed. Dinner with Drew Peloubet\, Board Chair\
 , and Bill Orosz\, former Board Chair\; Martha Ortiz\, Vice Chair\, may joi
 n.\nTue Jul 7: 9:15 AM meet Tim Flanagan in the Four Seasons lobby. Confere
 nce room available until 2:00 PM\; Jason can leave whenever best for his fl
 ight. Tim will send a separate text with Dan's information.\nSpans the July
  4th holiday.\n\nView live: https://jstravelschedule.netlify.app
LOCATION:Philadelphia\, PA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
